{
	"id": "sveltekit-og-v5",
	"name": "SvelteKit OG 5 (next)",
	"repo": "ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"url": "https://github.com/ethercorps/sveltekit-og",
	"summary": "The 5.0.0-next pre-release of SvelteKit OG: one API on the server and in the browser, Takumi by default and Satori on request, each engine an optional peer the app installs.",
	"description": "The public API (one shared ImageResponse that the server and client entries extend, and options the engine field narrows) and the single render pipeline to a lazily loaded engine, stubbed when its peer is missing. v4 had a class and a render path per engine.",
	"notes": "No Engine interface exists: Engine is the union \"takumi\" | \"satori\" (an attribute type here, not drawn), the two engine modules share render(vnode, options) only by convention, serverPlatform/clientPlatform are const objects drawn as classes realizing Platform, and the stub is source text from plugin.stubSource, not a class. ResponseOptions is folded into ImageResponseOptions; unions narrowed (render results drawn Promise<Uint8Array>, svg actually yields a string; Satori format string = png or svg; FontInput also admits FontDescriptor). Left out for the 14 limit: core/packages.ts (installMessage), helpers/response.ts, the memoized providers and client wasm/font loaders, FONT_CACHE_MAP, resolveFonts, ErrorCodes.",
